{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>My Sabbaths you shall keep.</b> As Rashi explained. And even though He warned us the likes of this regarding the Tabernacle, He returned and warned also regarding the Temple, because it is holier and more fixed. And <b>My sanctuary you shall revere</b> — therefore do not turn to the ovot and the yid'oni practitioners, for what business do you have with ovot and yid'oni practitioners? Behold, you have a sanctuary in which are Urim and Tummim. Another interpretation: <b>and My sanctuary you shall revere</b> — the commandment of My holiness. All the commandments are called in the language of holiness. And a proof for this matter is in the passage below: למען טמא את מקדשי — which is the language of holiness — ולחלל את שם קדשי — after it a doubling of the word, and one should not explain it as the language of the Temple building itself, for what defilement of the Temple is there in passing one's seed to Molech?"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The Hebrew אבות here refers to אוב practitioners of necromancy, paired with ידעונים; both are rendered according to their standard halakhic-cultic sense."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:41.798036290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}